From 7f19e408fae54608ddc522980e4cbbe3018b09eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:45:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Weekly pipeline: Dropbox importer in /admin, emailed pack
 links with lead log, three access levels per file

- Report files: access is now open / request (in the pack, behind the email form) / internal (never shown or served)
- Email gate: /api/request-pack logs the request, emails the reader an expiring link (/research/pack/<token>) and tells info@ plus the territory's partner; downloads are short-lived signed URLs; opens and downloads are counted
- /admin/import: one-time Dropbox connection (read-only), lists weekly manifests from the publishing folder, imports each territory as drafts or publishes; idempotent; live entries protected; a study never publishes with a file missing
- /admin/requests: who asked for which study, and whether they opened it
- Scans link to the study they led to, and studies link back; week label on both
- Study page lists only files a reader may have; Executive Visual shown at natural size
- supabase/004_weekly_pipeline.sql, docs/WEEKLY_PIPELINE.md, .env.example
